    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.clue\n\n### Description\n\nThere is a strange `gs` mapping described as `Sleep` in `mini.clue` source code. But there is no such mapping in any \"standard nvim\" or even \"mini\" setups. Most probably some copy-pasting form local. However, this makes me wonder are there any similar bugs? I mean similar misleading mappings that don't exist.\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.10\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nhttps://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/lua/mini/clue.lua#L748 or search \"Sleep\" in `mini.clue` code.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n_No response_\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nThere should be no `gs` mapping. Maybe other mappings need a quick sanity look as well.",
